Hi {{adjuster_name}},

I'm requesting a reinspection on the claim for {{client_name}} ({{claim_number}}). During review, we identified the following that we don't believe was captured in the original inspection:

- {{disputed_item_1}}
- {{disputed_item_2}}

I've attached supporting photos/documentation. Could we get this scheduled? Happy to work around your availability.

Thanks,
{{your_name}}

Hi {{recipient_name}},

To move forward on the claim for {{claim_number}}, I need the following:

- {{item_needed_1}}
- {{item_needed_2}}

This will help us {{why_it_matters}}. Let me know if you have any questions, or if there's anything I can do to help get this together.

Thanks,
{{your_name}}

Re: Request for Reconsideration – Claim {{claim_number}}
Insured: {{client_name}}
Property: {{property_address}}
Date of Loss: {{date_of_loss}}

{{adjuster_name}},

We are in receipt of Allstate's {{denial_date}} response declining to extend the repair beyond the directly damaged area on the basis that "there is no matching coverage in Illinois." We respectfully request that Allstate reconsider. The issue here is not an optional upgrade for appearance; it is whether Allstate has paid to put the property back with material of like kind and quality. The independent ITEL report shows it cannot be done with a partial repair.

1. The ITEL report is independent evidence that no matching material is available.
ITEL report #{{itel_report_number}} ({{itel_report_date}}), a third-party lab analysis of a sample taken from this roof, found that the existing {{material_description}} is {{itel_finding}} (for example: discontinued, with no available product that matches in color, profile, dimension, and exposure). The closest available product, {{closest_match_product}}, differs in {{mismatch_specifics}}. No other material evidence in the file contradicts this. If Allstate believes a matching product exists, please identify it by manufacturer, product line, color, and a current supplier so we can verify it. Otherwise, the ITEL finding stands unrebutted.

2. The Allstate policy itself requires like kind and quality.
The policy's replacement cost provision ({{policy_form_and_section}}) obligates Allstate to pay to repair or replace damaged property with materials of like kind and quality [replace with the exact quoted language from the declarations/policy form]. A repair that uses visibly different shingles does not restore the property to like kind and quality. Allstate's position does not rest on a matching exclusion. We are not asking for coverage that does not exist; we are asking Allstate to honor the replacement cost promise it already made. Courts applying Illinois law have read similar "comparable material and quality" wording to require replacing undamaged material when the replacement would not reasonably match. See Windridge of Naperville Condo. Ass'n v. Philadelphia Indem. Ins. Co., 932 F.3d 1035 (7th Cir. 2019).

3. Request for the specific policy basis.
If Allstate maintains its position, please identify in writing the specific policy provision (form number, page, and language) that Allstate relies on to exclude replacement needed to restore like kind and quality, and explain how the ITEL findings were considered. A general statement that matching is not covered in Illinois does not identify a policy basis. Illinois claims-handling rules require a written denial to identify the specific policy definition, limitation, exclusion, or condition it relies on. (50 Ill. Adm. Code 919.50(a)(1))

Requested action:
- Revise the estimate to include replacement of {{requested_scope}} (the full roof / affected elevations) so the result has a reasonably uniform appearance.
- Or provide a written response within {{response_days}} days that identifies the policy language relied on and the specific matching product Allstate contends is available.

Attached: ITEL report #{{itel_report_number}}; photos of the sample location and the existing roof; the contractor estimate; any manufacturer discontinuation notice.

The insured reserves all rights under the policy, including the appraisal provision. If this cannot be resolved, we will ask the insured to consider filing a complaint with the Illinois Department of Insurance.

Thank you,
{{your_name}}
{{company_name}}
On behalf of and with the written authorization of {{client_name}}
